 Generalized bicycle codes, which are a special case of  abelian  2GBA codes (and therefore of lifted product codes). Here the group is chosen as the cyclic group of order  l , and the base matrices  a  and  b  are the sum of the group algebra elements corresponding to the shifts  a_shifts  and  b_shifts . Behind the scenes, the shifts are converted to the corresponding group algebra elements and piped to  two_block_group_algebra_code . See also:  two_block_group_algebra_code ,  bicycle_code_as_2bga . Examples A [[254, 28, 14 ≤ d ≤ 20]] code from (A1) in Appendix B of ( Panteleev and Kalachev, 2021 ). julia> import Hecke; using QuantumClifford.ECC

